      "abstract": "This article follows the global career of the concept of \u2018worldview\u2019 from 1790 to the present, from its origin in German Idealism to its translation and transposition to the UK, the Netherlands, and North and South America. By integrating conceptual history within a sociological model based on apologetics, the article explores the formative power of culture wars in the intellectual and religious life of the past two centuries. It argues that within this apologetic framework different social movements\u2013comprised of scientific secularists, orthodox Christians, liberal skeptics, followers of political ideologies, or indigenous activists\u2013coalesced around divergent definitions of worldview. Worldview helped structure their movements, while providing a means for understanding and counteracting opponents. The apologetics of worldview offers a new approach to the joint history of the secular and religious and provides essential findings for scholars now using worldview and related concepts, such as ontology, for social scientific analysis.",
